{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates price levels by 5-10 EUR when the market is in a downtrend (e.g., Jan 2024), failing to capture the depth of the decline.",
    "Correct for severe upward bias: The model consistently underestimates price levels by 5-10 EUR when the market is in an uptrend (e.g., Apr-May 2024), failing to capture the magnitude of the rally.",
    "Eliminate flat-line forecasting: The model exhibits excessive inertia, predicting near-constant prices or linear trends regardless of high volatility or sentiment shifts; forecasts must be made more responsive to recent price momentum.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag: Positive sentiment spikes (e.g., 1.00) are not immediately reflected in the forecast; apply an immediate upward adjustment to the first 3-5 days of the forecast horizon following a strong positive sentiment signal.",
    "Account for mean reversion speed: The model is too slow to revert to the mean after price spikes; reduce the forecast slope in the 10-20 day horizon following a sharp price increase to match the observed faster reversion in true outcomes."
  ]
}
